  <prompt>Owner 2026-11-27 decision D-233 (notes/decisions.md): option A on #3279. Read gh issue view 3279, gh issue view 1984 and DI-179. PR #3273 (task 228) added a 409 inquiry.disposition_required to PATCH /api/v1/child-records/sprk_todo/{id} (ChildRecordEndpoints InquiryTodoCloseRefusalAsync). (1) Route SmartTodo's updateTodoStatus and dismissTodo (src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/services/TodoDataverseService.ts ~:98-111) and the LegalWorkspace To Do block's complete/dismiss through that BFF PATCH (existing authenticatedFetch from @spaarke/auth; no new endpoint), and show the refusal in plain words ("Record the outcome on the inquiry first"). (2) Add the same InquiryTodoCloseRefusalAsync check to the chat update tool (src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Handlers/DataverseUpdateRecordHandler.cs ~:195-215) before its confirm dialog, reusing the guard, not copying it. (3) The model-driven form Deactivate stays a known limit (ADR-002, no plugins): note it in the PR. Run /conflict-check first (shared library used by several projects).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE full-stack developer: React 19 shared components, @spaarke/auth, .NET 10 BFF AI tool handlers.</role>
  <goal>Completing or dismissing an open inquiry's outcome To Do from SmartTodo Kanban, the LegalWorkspace To Do block or the chat tool is refused in plain words; every other To Do closes as before.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Moving SmartTodo writes to the BFF changes the path for every To Do status change: keep the result identical for To Dos with no open inquiry (same statecode/statuscode, same UI refresh), handle offline/failed calls as the current Xrm path does, and do not break hosts that load SmartTodo without the BFF configured (check every host; if any lacks the BFF, STOP and report). Notify the SmartTodo and LegalWorkspace owners via the PR. A real Dataverse create and read is required before merge (push-to-github Step 1.7): do it on dev and record it in the notes (no ids in public). Run /conflict-check; read git log -5 on the files you edit.</background>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §6 gotcha 2026-11-24">Run the relevant --filter (Signals code: "FullyQualifiedName~Signals", which includes the contract baselines; Communication: "FullyQualifiedName~Communication"; Ai: "FullyQualifiedName~Ai"); update any baseline the change moves in the same PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §10">BFF hygiene when the BFF changes: publish-size delta vs a fresh master build (short paths, same zip tool, file counts) in the PR; no new HIGH CVE; no new package.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §11">No new service, interface, endpoint or DI registration unless the three questions are answered in the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md §6">Filtered BFF tests only (never the unfiltered Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests); full ArchTests (build tests/Spaarke.ArchTests explicitly first). Client code: run node scripts/quality/client-lint/client-lint.mjs check and the package jest suite.</constraint>
    <constraint source="public repo">No environment GUIDs, user or contact ids, mailbox addresses, tenant names or private access-control mechanics in code, tests, notes, commits or the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md §2 / D-106">Fix only what the named issues describe. Any other defect found: report it in the task notes and to the main session; do not fix it here.</constraint>
  </constraints>
